  "question": {
    "text": "Equation of common tangent of $y=x^2, y=-x^2+4 x-4$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "J4Kd3",
      "text": "\n$y=4(x-1)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "jorSl",
      "text": "\n$y=0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "zvIao",
      "text": "\n$y=-4(x-1)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "fhu4t",
      "text": "\n$y=-30 x-50$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The equation of tangent to $y=x^2$, be $y=m x-\\frac{m^2}{4}$, putting in $y=-x^2+4 x-4$, we should only get one value of $x$ i.e. Discriminate must be zero.\n$$\n\\begin{array}{rrr}\n\\therefore & m x-\\frac{m^2}{4} & =-x^2+4 x-4 \\\\\n\\Rightarrow & x^2+x(m-4)+4-\\frac{m^2}{4} & =0 \\\\\n\\Rightarrow & m(m-4) & =0 \\\\\n& \\therefore y=0 & \\text { or } m=0,4\n\\end{array}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\therefore y=0 \\text { and } y=4(x-1) \\text { are tangents. }\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
